<div class="lens-concrete-example lifecycle-example" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{EXAMPLE_PREFIX}}-title">
<p class="lens-overline">{{LIFECYCLE_ICON}}<span>Lifecycle in the incident</span></p><h3 id="{{EXAMPLE_PREFIX}}-title">Read each state and its route for change</h3>
<p class="incident-flow-intro">At ticket {{CASE_TICKET_ID}}’s latest checkpoint, read these four parallel tracks. Each shows a current state, a possible next state or replacement, the required conditions and the effect if that change is completed.</p>
<ol class="incident-state-tracks" role="list" aria-label="Four independent incident state tracks and their change conditions">
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="incident-state-content"><h4>Completeness definition · version {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}}</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Definition acceptance track</span>
<div class="incident-state-route"><div><span class="record-label">Current</span><strong>Accepted (admitted)</strong><span>Governs this export assessment scope</span></div><span class="incident-state-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="record-label">Possible next</span><strong>Superseded</strong><span>An admitted successor is selected</span></div></div>
<dl class="incident-state-conditions"><div><dt>What must happen</dt><dd>Validate and review the successor meaning. An authorized human owner must admit that exact version and issue a successor decision naming it as the replacement.</dd></div><div><dt>Effect if completed</dt><dd>Current lookup selects the successor. Version {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}}, its earlier acceptance and its evidence remain identifiable.</dd></div></dl>
</div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="incident-state-content"><h4>Proposed code · revision {{CASE_FIX_REVISION}}</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Implementation record lifecycle</span>
<div class="incident-state-route"><div><span class="record-label">Current</span><strong>Candidate record</strong><span>Efficacy still needs assessment</span></div><span class="incident-state-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="record-label">Possible next</span><strong>Active record</strong><span>Only under its declared lifecycle</span></div></div>
<dl class="incident-state-conditions"><div><dt>What must happen</dt><dd>Evaluate the exact revision against its implementation contract, preserve conformance evidence and obtain the owner’s authorization for the specified record transition.</dd></div><div><dt>Effect if completed</dt><dd>The implementation record becomes active within the approved scope. Adoption for use, deployment and running-service activation keep their own decisions and execution evidence.</dd></div></dl>
</div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="incident-state-content"><h4>Incident response · {{CASE_TICKET_ID}}</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Response closure track · incident record currently active</span>
<div class="incident-state-route"><div><span class="record-label">Current</span><strong>Open response</strong><span>Cause and recovery unestablished</span></div><span class="incident-state-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="record-label">Possible next</span><strong>Closed response</strong><span>Owner-authorized closure</span></div></div>
<dl class="incident-state-conditions"><div><dt>What must happen</dt><dd>The accountable owner reviews the assessment, containment and recovery posture, communications, uncertainty and follow-up obligations under the incident’s Policy, then authorizes closure if its conditions are met.</dd></div><div><dt>Effect if completed</dt><dd>The response closure field changes. Failure Occurrences, unresolved cause, evidence and remaining obligations are preserved. The incident record’s lifecycle is governed separately.</dd></div></dl>
</div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="incident-state-content"><h4>Task information · view {{CASE_VIEW_VERSION}}</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Context View usability track</span>
<div class="incident-state-route"><div><span class="record-label">Current</span><strong>Expired view {{CASE_VIEW_VERSION}}</strong><span>Agent work is paused</span></div><span class="incident-state-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="record-label">Replacement</span><strong>New usable view</strong><span>Resolved and checked for this task</span></div></div>
<dl class="incident-state-conditions"><div><dt>What must happen</dt><dd>Resolve a new view against the intended Context and exact source epoch. Check its sources, digests, coverage, limitations and use conditions. Confirm that the agent’s delegation is still current.</dd></div><div><dt>Effect if completed</dt><dd>The new immutable view supplies usable task information; view {{CASE_VIEW_VERSION}} retains its history. Resuming work also requires current permission. Producing a view does not extend the delegation window.</dd></div></dl>
</div></li>
</ol>
<div class="incident-flow-boundary"><strong>Apply only the effects authorized for that track.</strong><p>The definition’s authority, the evidence for the omission, the code record’s state, the incident’s closure and the agent’s permission remain separately reported. Every completed change records its exact subject, decision or required checks, and resulting state.</p></div>
<details class="incident-flow-details"><summary>How the definition reached its current state</summary>
<p>Before this incident, the owner took definition {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}} through the example’s declared Definition profile. Each completed transition had its own gate and effect.</p>
<ol class="definition-history-flow" role="list"><li><strong>Written · candidate-authored</strong><p>To become <em>validated-candidate</em>, the exact candidate must pass its bound evaluation profile. The resulting state records validation.</p></li><li><strong>Validated · validated-candidate</strong><p>To become <em>owner-reviewed</em>, the owner must review the exact candidate digest and evidence set. The resulting state records review completion.</p></li><li><strong>Owner reviewed · owner-reviewed</strong><p>To become <em>admitted</em>, an authorized human admission decision must bind the exact candidate, evidence, registry selection, index and drift review. The selected version becomes authoritative within its scope.</p></li><li><strong>Accepted · admitted</strong><p>An exact successor decision selecting an admitted replacement can make it <em>superseded</em>. An authorized withdrawal decision with a replacement or terminal route can make it <em>withdrawn</em>, removing current authority while preserving history. Earlier candidate states may also be withdrawn through their declared owner route.</p></li></ol>
<div class="example-formal-result"><code>x = completeness definition {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}}</code><code>C = its declared Definition lifecycle profile</code><code>s = owner-reviewed; t = admitted</code></div>
<p>The prior acceptance met those conditions and made this version govern the assessment. These service examples illustrate the Lab’s separations; exact transition gates and effects come from each subject’s applicable profile or Policy.</p>
</details>
</div>
